* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-dialectics.wav|a=US}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{uder|en|grc|διαλεκτική||the art of argument through interactive questioning and answering}}, from {{m|grc|διαλεκτικός||competent debater}}, from {{m|grc|διαλέγομαι||to participate in a [[dialogue]]}}, from {{m|grc|διά||inter, through}} + {{m|grc|λέγειν||to speak}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|philosophy|uncountable}} A [[systematic]] method of [[argument]] that attempts to [[resolve]] the [[contradiction]]s in [[opposing]] [[view]]s or [[idea]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The '''dialectics''' of absolute and relative, concrete and abstract, subject and object, and theory and practice is focused on some of the most important questions in philosophy.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1880|author=w:Friedrich Engels|chapter=2| title=[https://www.marxists.org/archive/marx/works/1880/soc-utop/index.htm Socialism: Utopian and Scientific]| passage=None of these processes and modes of thought enters into the framework of [[metaphysical]] reasoning. '''Dialectics''', on the other hand, comprehends things and their representations, ideas, in their essential connection, concatenation, motion, origin and ending. Such processes as those mentioned above are, therefore, so many corroborations of its own method of procedure.}}

